{
  "name": "Send a weekly Google Analytics 4 report with AI insights via Gmail",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Send a weekly Google Analytics 4 report with AI insights via Gmail\n\nGet a clear weekly website report in your inbox every Monday without opening Google Analytics. The workflow pulls last week's GA4 numbers and the week before, calculates the changes, and asks Google Gemini to write a short headline, wins, concerns and next actions in plain English. The numbers in the table come straight from GA4; the AI only writes the commentary.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Every Monday at 8am** starts the run; **Set report settings** holds your property ID and email.\n2. Four Google Analytics nodes fetch this week's and last week's users, sessions, page views, engaged sessions and key events, plus top pages and traffic sources.\n3. **Calculate week-over-week changes** totals each metric and works out percentage changes.\n4. **Write insights with AI** returns a headline, wins, concerns and actions as JSON.\n5. **Build report email** renders a tidy HTML table with green and red arrows and **Send report via Gmail** delivers it.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add a **Google Analytics OAuth2** credential (enable the Google Analytics Data API in Google Cloud) and select it on the four GA4 nodes.\n2. Add a free **Google Gemini (PaLM) API** credential and a **Gmail OAuth2** credential.\n3. In **Set report settings**, replace `YOUR_GA4_PROPERTY_ID` (Admin > Property details, numbers only), your site name and `YOUR_EMAIL_ADDRESS`.\n4. Run it once manually, then activate.\n\n### Customization\n- Swap `keyEvents` for a specific conversion, or add metrics in the GA4 nodes and **Calculate week-over-week changes**.\n\nFailure alerts: fill in the alert node in **Alert on errors** and choose this workflow under **Settings > Error workflow**.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 600
      },
